.615 E at 11.4 kilometers, moving toward 282.12 degrees, about west-northwest, on a shallow slope of 17.48 degrees. Speed is 19.65 kilometers per second with an uncertainty of 0.29 kilometers per second; companion estimate 19.07 kilometers per second confirms consistency. Because even the lower bound exceeds Earth escape speed, a natural object is solid.\n\nUncertainty remains small on slope and exact endpoint. Missing are later dark-flight data and recovered fragments, so final descent and strewn field are not constrained.","run":{"run_id":"20261027T132419-a996","status":"approved","block":null,"git":{"commit":"ca005ff","dirty":true},"planner":"native","planner_model":"muse-spark-1.3","cost_usd":0.1316,"reports":{"es":{"check":{"passed":true,"numbers":17,"traced":17,"orphans":[],"hemisphere_mismatches":[]}},"en":{"check":{"passed":true,"numbers":16,"traced":16,"orphans":[],"hemisphere_mismatches":[]}}},"history":[{"at":"2026-10-27T13:55:00","review":"approved","by":"Diego Burbano","notes":null}]},"grade":{"passed":"4 of 5","gate":{"azimuth":true,"slope":true,"flare_height":true,"end_point":true,"speed_29_oct":false}}}